WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.868
-The president gave a speech

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:03.903
to a group of Republicans
last night.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.204
where he sent a bunch
of insane stuff.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:07.106
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.976
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.645
-It's been almost two weeks

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.881
since Trump's attorney general
released a memo

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.083
in Special Counsel
Robert Mueller's final report.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.253
The memo said Mueller had not
established a conspiracy

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.821
between the Trump campaign
and Russia,

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.857
but it also said Mueller
had not exonerated Trump

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:27.493
of obstruction of justice,
so it was a mixed bag.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.328
But Trump has declared
himself victorious

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:30.497
and even threatened last week

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.099
to keep the full report hidden
from the public.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.733
-The president --
the same president,

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:36.202
who over the past week has said

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.906
he's for the full release
of the report wrote this --

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.207
"The problem is,
no matter what

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.741
the radical-left Democrats get,

00:00:42.741 --> 00:00:45.411
no matter what we give them it,
it will never be enough.

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.546
Just watch.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.581
They will harass
and complain and resist

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.049
the theme of their movement.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:54.120
So, maybe we should just
take our victory and say no.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.821
We've got a country to run.

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:58.624
-Okay, first of all,
you don't have a country to run

00:00:58.624 --> 00:00:59.858
because you don't run it.

00:00:59.858 --> 00:01:02.661
You outsource it to
your collection of weirdos

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:06.732
while you go golfing
with Kid Rock.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.101
By the way, I'm glad.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.836
I'm glad to see Kid Rock
is respecting the flag

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:13.139
by turning it
into a fart catcher.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.108
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.009
In fact, despite
proclaiming falsely

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.211
that he's been exonerated,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.946
some officials even
within the White House

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.448
are anxious that the president
is getting ahead of himself

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.916
before the full report
comes out.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:27.353
One senior White House official
said, "There will be plenty

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.488
of unfavorable things
about the president

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:30.989
in the full report,
which we think

00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:32.324
will eventually come out,

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:35.060
so let's not go overboard
saying there's no wrongdoing.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.262
Let's move on."

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.463
Yeah, of course,

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:39.865
there will be damning things
in the report,

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:42.702
because we know publicly
it's damning.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.704
Mueller's report could
literally just be

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.438
a bunch of news articles
about Trump

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:47.907
stapled together
with a cover sheet

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.876
that says,
"Remember this stuff?"

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.477
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:52.912
And while...

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:56.415
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.551
While Trump, himself,

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.186
wants to declare victory
and move on,

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.887
he also seems stuck
on his obsession

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:03.789
with how Mueller's investigation
got started.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.090
The answer to that is simple.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.059
The FBI was investigating
his ties to Russia

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:09.194
and then he fired the guy
in charge of that investigation

00:02:09.194 --> 00:02:11.063
and because his
of Republican attorney general

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.198
had recused himself,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.066
his Republican
deputy attorney general

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:15.502
appointed Robert Mueller.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:18.071
But Trump still wants someone
to look into what he called

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:21.074
or what he tried to call
"the origins of the report."

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.176
But he sad some trouble
saying the word.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:26.078
I hope they now go and take
a look at the oranges --

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:29.949
the origins
of the investigation,

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.051
the beginnings
of that investigation.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.721
You look at the origin
of the investigation.

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:40.159
The Mueller report, I wish,
covered the oranges...

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.194
how it started.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:44.831
-"Yeah. Hey, mom...

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:49.168
Mom, I'm worried about grandpa."

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.869
Yeah.

00:02:50.869 --> 00:02:52.471
Yeah, oranges."

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.107
[ Laughter ]
Why does he keep saying oranges?

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:58.745
Is he hungry or is that
always how he says it?

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.046
[ As Trump ]
Did you see "Captain Marvel"?

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.382
It is pretty good
for an oranges story.

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.983
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.250
[ Normal voice ]
And if you're confused by this,

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.053
you're not the only one --
even the White House

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.188
can't figure out
what Trump was trying to say,

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.490
because in their official
transcript of his remarks,

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.593
the transcript that is published
on the White House website,

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:16.529
They had to invent a new word.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.097
Here is how they spelled it.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.999
"I hope they now go

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:23.035
and take a look at the oranges."

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:25.071
I love imagining
the stenographer

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.738
who had to type that one out.

00:03:26.738 --> 00:03:28.374
"Take a look at the...

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:32.378
I don't know."
Just make something up.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.514
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:41.220
That looks how a child
would spell it

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.689
on a piece of cardboard

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.924
if they opened up
their own fruit stand.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:47.727
[ Laughter ]
I mean, seriously, though.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:48.795
Is...

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.733
Is the White House going do this

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.468
every time Trump
makes up a new word?

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.836
I mean, what about this one.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.806
-God bless the United "Shtates."

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.641
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:04.043
Does that mean they are going

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:07.413
to have to change the signs
at the airport?

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:12.051
And while Trump's hung up

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.153
on the oranges
of the investigation

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.555
his supporters, like
Fox News host Jeanine Pirro,

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.024
are hung up
on a different obsession.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.659
They want everyone associated
with the report to go to jail,

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:23.328
although I have to say,
the way she ended her rant

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:25.965
made it a lot less dramatic
than she intended.

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.901
-This should never happen again,

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.304
and I can guarantee you
it will happen again

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:35.140
unless we make an example
of the traitorous,

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.876
treasonous group
that accused Donald Trump

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:40.612
of being an agent
of the Russian government.

00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:42.581
These arrogant, lying,

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:43.883
condescending, leaking,

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.885
haters of you and me

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:49.555
and the America
that doesn't have power

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:53.526
are going to do it again
unless we stop them

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.494
and the only way to stop them

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:58.830
is with justice --
true justice --

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:03.136
and that's
behind-the-bars justice.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.539
And that's my open.

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.741
Let me know what you think
on my Facebook and Twitter.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.843
#JudgeJeanine.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:13.646
-Now, it really undercuts
your authoritarian call

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.014
for traitors to be
thrown in jail

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:18.884
when you end it by asking people
to like you on Facebook.

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.886
You never saw Stalin
get on TV and say,

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.488
"We will crush the opposition

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.390
and root out the traitors
amongst us.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.926
And, as always, please remember,
like and subscribe."

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.628
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.628 --> 00:05:33.265
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.100
So, it's been almost two weeks
since Mueller's report

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.402
was delivered,
and in that time,

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.836
the question on everybody's mind
has been,

00:05:37.836 --> 00:05:38.904
how would Trump respond?

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.339
Would this strengthen him
politically?

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:41.741
What message would he focus on?

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:42.942
And now we have the answer,

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.510
as we learned at a rally
last week

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.844
and again in the speech
last night

00:05:45.844 --> 00:05:47.947
Trump has decided to spend
the rest of his presidency

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:50.550
doing the impressions
of windmills.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.684
-If Hillary got in,
you wouldn't have that stat.

00:05:52.684 --> 00:05:54.620
I can tell you right now.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.656
You'd be doing wind.
You can be doing windmills.

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:57.724
Whee.

00:05:57.724 --> 00:06:01.026
Hillary wanted
to put up wind, wind.

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:04.297
If you have a windmill
anywhere near your house,

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.531
congratulations --

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.901
your house just went down
75% in value.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:12.472
and they say the noise
causes cancer.

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:13.973
You tell me that one, okay?

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:16.041
[ Imitates whirring sound ]

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.210
-So many questions.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:21.914
First, the idea that
noise from windmills

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.050
causes cancer is insane,
but, second,

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:28.620
why does his impression
keep clanging.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.990
-Whee!
[ Imitates whirring sound ]

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.091
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.459
-[ As Trump ] You know, cats?

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:37.496
Cats -- they're either like meow
or woof, woof, woof, woof.

00:06:37.496 --> 00:06:39.865
[ Scattered applause ]

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:44.170
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.572
[ Normal voice ] Trump's riff
on cancer-causing windmills

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:47.740
was only the beginning.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.242
He also told the Republicans
in attendance

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.609
they say they should
be more careful

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:52.544
about voter fraud,
which is nonexistent.

00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:55.781
In fact, the most prominent case
of election fraud in 2018

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:57.450
was committed by a Republican
in North Carolina,

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:01.086
but Trump kept insisting
that something was going on.

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:02.688
-You got to watch
those vote tallies.

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:05.524
You know, I keep hearing
about the election

00:07:05.524 --> 00:07:07.526
and the various

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:10.095
counting measures
that they have.

00:07:10.095 --> 00:07:12.932
There were a lot of close
elections that were --

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:15.367
they seemed, to every
single one of them,

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:16.902
went Democrat.

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:19.472
If it was close,
they say the Democrat --

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.839
There's something
going on, fella.

00:07:20.839 --> 00:07:24.911
Hey, you to be little bit
more paranoid than you are.

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:25.912
Okay?

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:27.980
-More paranoid?!

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.417
You already think windmills
are causing cancer.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:33.485
The only way you can
be more paranoid

00:07:33.485 --> 00:07:37.222
is if you thought the windmills
were committing voter fraud.

00:07:37.222 --> 00:07:39.425
[ As Trump ] The windmills --
they're wearing disguises,

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:41.827
and they're voting --
oh, they're voting!

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:43.229
I saw one in a polling booth.

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:45.831
Big hat, mustache.

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.800
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.771
[ Speaks gibberish ]

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:56.442
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:57.976
[ Normal voice ] Trump
also expressed concern

00:07:57.976 --> 00:07:59.311
in that same speech

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:02.181
that his remarks would
get out to the press.

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.016
Trump is talking about
something incomprehensible

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.551
that's honestly not even
worth explaining.

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:07.487
The important part
is the end of the clip.

00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:10.923
They put names,
and you pick a name.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:13.692
Ladies and gentlemen,
I'm proud to announce so and so.

00:08:13.692 --> 00:08:15.394
I don't want to use names
'cause I'll get in trouble.

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:18.931
Somebody's going to leak this
whole damn speech to the media.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:22.001
-Leak it to the media?
You're on TV!

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:23.803
[ Laughter ]
You're not...

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:26.939
Do you not see the cameras?

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.507
Do you not see the cameras?

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:30.776
I can't believe I had to say it.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:33.379
You should be more paranoid.

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.046
You're the president
of the United States,

00:08:35.046 --> 00:08:35.948
and you're on television.

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:38.050
We can all see you.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.452
You're like a guy live-streaming
himself on Facebook,

00:08:40.452 --> 00:08:44.022
screaming, "I'm being watched."

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:47.959
I mean, I'm worried someone
is going to leak this,

00:08:47.959 --> 00:08:49.228
and he's going to see it.

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:53.732
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.732 --> 00:08:56.135
In fact, Trump was
so afraid to use names

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:59.305
that when he after Congresswoman
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez,

00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:01.307
who proposed the Green New Deal,

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:03.242
he referred to her
by her previous job,

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:04.576
instead of the current one.

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:06.078
-The Green New Deal

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:09.382
done by a young bartender,
29 years old.

00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:11.216
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.216 --> 00:09:13.552
A young bartender.
-All right.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.287
First of all,
she is a member of Congress

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:17.689
and her name is
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.

00:09:17.689 --> 00:09:21.394
[ Cheers and applause ]
I mean...

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.098
We call you "Mr. President,"

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:29.435
not Crazy Windmill Cancer Guy.

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:31.470
It's like, so what
if she was a bartender?

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.172
We need more working people
and women of color in politics.

00:09:34.172 --> 00:09:37.642
Right now,
every Senate hearing --

00:09:37.642 --> 00:09:39.244
Right now,
every Senate hearing

00:09:39.244 --> 00:09:40.645
looks like
a Clint Eastwood movie,

00:09:40.645 --> 00:09:43.916
where a bunch of old guys
decide to pull one last heist.

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:45.551
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:48.086
Whether you agree
with the details or not,

00:09:48.086 --> 00:09:50.789
AOC has an ambitious plan
to deal with an existential

00:09:50.789 --> 00:09:52.224
threat to the planet,
and she's got everyone

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.291
talking about climate change.

00:09:53.291 --> 00:09:54.426
Trump, on the other hand,

00:09:54.426 --> 00:09:56.361
tried to explain
his trade policy last night,

00:09:56.361 --> 00:09:59.298
especially when it comes
to countries that sell us cars,

00:09:59.298 --> 00:10:00.800
and it made no sense whatsoever.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.468
-I said, if you don't do this,
we're gonna tariff every product

00:10:03.468 --> 00:10:06.138
coming out of your country
at 25%.

00:10:06.138 --> 00:10:07.773
And every time I had a problem,

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:10.643
I would just take, you know --
especially cars.

00:10:10.643 --> 00:10:13.011
I had a little plastic car
on my desk,

00:10:13.011 --> 00:10:14.613
and I'd have the leaders
come over,

00:10:14.613 --> 00:10:16.882
and I'd just take the car out,
put it on the front of the desk.

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:18.283
They'd say,
"Okay. We agree."

00:10:18.283 --> 00:10:20.019
-I do not believe that story.

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:21.153
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:23.288
-You take out
a little plastic --

00:10:23.288 --> 00:10:24.924
How does that even work?

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:27.893
"Mr. President, we have a trade
deficit of $800 billion."

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:31.597
[ As Trump ] Counterpoint.

00:10:31.597 --> 00:10:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:39.805
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:43.041 --> 00:10:44.543
And while Trump
rallies about windmills

00:10:44.543 --> 00:10:46.478
and attacks the Green New Deal,
the Democratic primary,

00:10:46.478 --> 00:10:48.114
on the other hand,
has been very policy focused.

00:10:48.114 --> 00:10:50.549
The candidates are talking about
everything from climate change

00:10:50.549 --> 00:10:51.817
to health care to voting rights.

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:53.785
In fact, today,
Senator Elizabeth Warren

00:10:53.785 --> 00:10:55.220
unveiled a bill
to make it easier

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.022
to jail executives
for company abuses,

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:59.524
And when she was asked
at a recent town hall

00:10:59.524 --> 00:11:00.993
about her plans
to increase taxes

00:11:00.993 --> 00:11:02.161
on the wealthiest Americans,

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:04.062
she could not contain
her excitement.

00:11:04.062 --> 00:11:06.298
-Thank you, Senator Warren,
for being here.

00:11:06.298 --> 00:11:08.867
How do you plan to make sure
the extremely rich

00:11:08.867 --> 00:11:10.102
pay their fair taxes?

00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:11.603
-Whoa!

00:11:11.603 --> 00:11:13.772
[ Laugher ]
-Damn!

00:11:13.772 --> 00:11:19.111
She reacted like she just
landed a rover on Mars.

00:11:19.111 --> 00:11:21.347
Elizabeth Warren reacts
to taxing the rich

00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:23.749
the way the rest of us
react to a surprise party.

00:11:23.749 --> 00:11:25.951
"Surprise!"
-Whoa!

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:27.285
[ Laughter ]

00:11:27.285 --> 00:11:28.820
She's excited to talk about it
because whether

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:30.856
you agree with it or not,
people want to hear about it.

00:11:30.856 --> 00:11:33.159
They don't really care that much
about Mueller or Russia.

00:11:33.159 --> 00:11:35.060
In fact, the website
FiveThirtyEight

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.262
found this week that Trump
hadn't seen a post-Mueller boost

00:11:37.262 --> 00:11:39.665
in the polls, in part,
because the Russia investigation

00:11:39.665 --> 00:11:41.399
isn't a big priority for voters.

00:11:41.399 --> 00:11:43.368
Most people have more
immediate worries,

00:11:43.368 --> 00:11:45.871
like whether they have
enough gas in the car

00:11:45.871 --> 00:11:47.206
or can pay their water bill,

00:11:47.206 --> 00:11:49.107
and tomorrow is
the kids' soccer game,

00:11:49.107 --> 00:11:50.476
and it's their turn to bring...

00:11:50.476 --> 00:11:51.877
-Oranges.

00:11:51.877 --> 00:11:56.248
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:58.250
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.351
Voters want to hear about stuff

00:11:59.351 --> 00:12:01.053
like healthcare
and climate change.

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:03.322
Trump doesn't have a plan to
deal with any of those issues.

00:12:03.322 --> 00:12:06.158
Instead, he's spending his time
rambling about windmills.

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:07.693
To get through the next
two years of this,

00:12:07.693 --> 00:12:08.928
We're all going to need
a really good...

00:12:08.928 --> 00:12:10.229
-Bartender.

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:12.197
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:12:12.197 --> 00:12:14.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

